263
00:12:42,050 --> 00:12:45,550
Too dry.

264
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,260
Do you believe in ghosts?

265
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,260
No.

266
00:12:47,470 --> 00:12:49,680
Is this movie gonna be my big break?

267
00:12:47,470 --> 00:12:49,680
No.

268
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:53,810
What?

269
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:53,810
Yes.

270
00:12:54,310 --> 00:12:57,100
Dude, you said no.

271
00:12:54,310 --> 00:12:57,100
I also said yes.

272
00:12:57,270 --> 00:12:59,310
You don't think this is gonna be a big break for me?

273
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:00,520
No.

274
00:13:03,490 --> 00:13:04,940
I don't believe this.

275
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:08,740
Look, Joe, I just don't want you to get your hopes up too high.

276
00:13:08,950 --> 00:13:11,950
What are you talking about? I'm the lead in a movie.

277
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:16,330
They're not even paying you. This doesn't even sound like a real movie.

278
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:19,580
You know, I don't know why you're dumping all over my big break.

279
00:13:19,790 --> 00:13:22,550
Because, Joe, I don't think this is going to be your big break.

280
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:25,550
Is that why you're on this trip? Huh? To make me feel like a loser?

281
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:28,640
Because if it is, I'd rather be alone.

282
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:28,640
You don't want me on the trip?

283
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,180
Not if you're like this.

284
00:13:30,430 --> 00:13:33,470
Tell you what, the next time you ask me a question like that, I'll lie.

285
00:13:33,770 --> 00:13:35,430
Yeah, I don't want you on the trip.

286
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:38,190
All right, fine. Why don't you pull over? I'll get out now.

287
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,600
Fine.

288
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,400
Get out.

289
00:13:43,610 --> 00:13:45,400
You're not supposed to stop on a bridge.

290
00:13:45,570 --> 00:13:47,450
Get out.

291
00:13:45,570 --> 00:13:47,450
Fine.

292
00:13:50,530 --> 00:13:52,910
Wait. Wait. There's no sidewalk.

293
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:55,580
Yeah. I'm gonna die here.

294
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:01,210
Okay, are you mad at me because my hair gel smells?

295
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,670
No.

296
00:14:03,590 --> 00:14:06,970
Are you angry with me because I said your handwriting is childlike?

297
00:14:07,170 --> 00:14:09,510
No, that made me feel precious.

298
00:14:10,390 --> 00:14:13,260
Oh, I know. Is it because he's always correcting people's grammar?

299
00:14:13,430 --> 00:14:16,770
You know, "whom, whom." Sometimes it's "who."

300
00:14:18,310 --> 00:14:20,190
Yeah? Sometimes it's...

301
00:14:23,190 --> 00:14:24,650
Oh, did you beat him at a board game?

302
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:27,280
He turns into such a baby when he starts to lose.

303
00:14:27,490 --> 00:14:30,660
Okay, I'm the baby.

304
00:14:27,490 --> 00:14:30,660
Hey. Stop it.

305
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,410
Hey.

306
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,410
What are you doing here?

307
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:37,080
Joey kicked me out of the car on the bridge.

308
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:39,370
Why?

309
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:39,370
I don't know. He went crazy.

310
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:43,130
We were playing that game where you ask a question and have to answer fast.

311
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:46,750
Oh, that game should not be played without my supervision.

312
00:14:48,130 --> 00:14:49,630
Well, I don't know what made him mad.

313
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:52,840
All I said was that, uh, I didn't think this was gonna be his big break...

314
00:14:53,010 --> 00:14:55,140
...that this movie wasn't gonna do anything for him...

315
00:14:55,310 --> 00:14:57,140
...and that it didn't sound like a real movie.

316
00:14:57,350 --> 00:15:00,140
Okay, he should've pushed me off the bridge.

317
00:15:00,350 --> 00:15:01,390
What's in the bag?

318
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,400
Oh, I figured you guys would all be mad at me...

319
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:06,320
...so I got you some gifts that I found on the side of the road.

320
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:09,320
Who wants the teddy bear with one leg?

321
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:09,320
I do.

322
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:14,700
Okay.

323
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:22,710
Not even close.

324
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:22,710
Okay, well, help me. I can't do this.

325
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:24,250
All right, come on. Let's do it.

326
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,040
All right.

327
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,040
Sit down.

328
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:29,210
All right, put your head back. All right.

329
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:29,210
Yes. Okay.

330
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:32,800
Now, open your eyes.

331
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:32,800
Okay, they are.

332
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:37,100
How many fingers am I holding up?

333
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:37,100
Four.

334
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:38,600
Oh, my God, I was thinking four.

335
00:15:38,810 --> 00:15:40,890
Really?

336
00:15:38,810 --> 00:15:40,890
Yes.

337
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:44,100
All right, why don't we start with a practice one, okay?

338
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,560
No drops.

339
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,560
Great.

340
00:15:47,270 --> 00:15:51,570
On three. One, two, three.

341
00:15:52,530 --> 00:15:53,910
My pillow's all wet.

342
00:15:54,110 --> 00:15:56,120
Well, you said it was practice.

343
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,990
Then why did you move?

344
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,990
Because I knew you were lying.

345
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:03,250
All right. Come here. Come on.

346
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:03,250
What are you doing? Monica.

347
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:05,580
Stop it! Oh, my God, stop it.

348
00:16:05,790 --> 00:16:07,670
I am going...

349
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:09,710
Turn it over.

350
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:09,710
Aah!

351
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:11,880
I am going to get...

352
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:15,010
Get these drops in your eye.

353
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:18,470
Oh, my God. You really are freakishly strong.

354
00:16:19,810 --> 00:16:23,060
Aah! Aah! Monica, stop it!

355
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:26,060
Damn, it's empty.

356
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:30,440
Wow. If Joey and Chandler walked in right now, we could make a fortune.

357
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:39,370
Ooh, that is definitely Chandler, Joey or Ross.

358
00:16:39,950 --> 00:16:40,990
Or Rachel.

359
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:45,920
Hello? It's Joey.

360
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:51,710
I'm so glad you called. Chandler told me what happened. He's really upset.

361
00:16:52,170 --> 00:16:56,760
Not as upset as he's gonna be when he finds out what I did with his sweater vests.

362
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:00,220
What did you do to his sweater vests?

363
00:17:00,430 --> 00:17:03,100
Let's just say there's a well-dressed pack of dogs in Ohio.

364
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:09,400
Monica, listen, is Phoebe there? I gotta ask her something about the car.

365
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,020
Yeah, hold on one second.

366
00:17:11,730 --> 00:17:13,780
Hey, dude.

367
00:17:11,730 --> 00:17:13,780
Hey, Pheebs.

368
00:17:13,990 --> 00:17:16,400
Listen, this wooden box keeps sliding out from under the seat.

369
00:17:16,570 --> 00:17:18,160
What is it?

370
00:17:16,570 --> 00:17:18,160
Oh, that's my grandma.

371
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:24,580
And thanks, Joey. She's having a really great time.

372
00:17:27,290 --> 00:17:29,130
Is that Joey? Is that Joey? Let me talk to him.

373
00:17:29,290 --> 00:17:31,210
Joey, Chandler's here. He was wondering if...

374
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:35,630
Okay, I guess he ran out of change.

375
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:37,380
He won't even talk to me.

376
00:17:37,550 --> 00:17:40,220
How am I gonna apologize to him if he won't even talk to me?

377
00:17:40,470 --> 00:17:42,010
Maybe you should send him something.

378
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:44,600
So when he gets to Las Vegas, he'll know that you're sorry.

379
00:17:44,810 --> 00:17:49,190
That's a good idea. I wonder where I could get a basket of porn?

380
00:17:50,190 --> 00:17:52,820
Oh, no, don't say I'm sorry with porn.

381
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:56,530
You know what you should send him? A carton of cigarettes.

382
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,740
Because that way he can trade it for protection.

383
00:17:58,910 --> 00:18:01,370
No. That's prison.

384
00:18:03,950 --> 00:18:05,080
Okay, Pheebs.

385
00:18:05,330 --> 00:18:07,080
I know how we're gonna figure this out.

386
00:18:07,250 --> 00:18:09,210
Okay. Clear your mind...

387
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:12,920
...and answer the first thing that comes into your head. Okay?

388
00:18:13,090 --> 00:18:14,210
Mm-hm.

389
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:16,670
What's better, flora or fauna?

390
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:16,670
Fauna.

391
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,380
Simon or Garfunkel?

392
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,380
Garfunkel.

393
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:21,260
Why are you mad at me?

394
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:21,260
You said I was boring. Oh.

395
00:18:24,260 --> 00:18:25,770
When did I say you were boring?

396
00:18:25,970 --> 00:18:29,060
Oh, my God, I remember now. We were playing chess.

397
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:32,230
Phoebe, you and I have never played chess.

398
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,480
Oh, come on. Yes.

399
00:18:33,650 --> 00:18:37,610
Remember that time on the frozen lake? We were playing. You said I was boring.

400
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:41,740
And then you took off your energy mask and you were Cameron Diaz.

401
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:47,330
Okay, there's a chance this may have been a dream.

402
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:19,070
Hey. Stanley. Hey.

403
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,030
Your leading man is here. Let's get to work.

404
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:25,370
Um, slight change of plans. We've shut down.

405
00:19:26,330 --> 00:19:27,490
What? Why?

406
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:30,000
It's a money thing. We don't have any.

407
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:34,750
Ha, ha. You're kidding, right?

408
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:34,750
No.

409
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:38,920
What?

410
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:38,920
It's probably just temporary.

411
00:19:39,170 --> 00:19:42,470
We're hoping to get more money soon, so if you could just, uh, hang out.

412
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:44,640
Hang out? How long?

413
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:48,560
I don't know. A week. Maybe two. The money'll turn up.

414
00:19:48,770 --> 00:19:52,190
People always wanna invest in movies. Hey, you're not rich, are you?

415
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,190
No.

416
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,190
Worth a shot.

417
00:19:56,060 --> 00:19:59,320
Well, Joey, let me know where you're staying, okay?

418
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:04,570
Hey, pal. Are you Joey Tribbiani?

419
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:04,570
Yeah.

420
00:20:04,820 --> 00:20:06,240
These got left for you.

421
00:20:06,490 --> 00:20:08,080
Thanks.

422
00:20:09,370 --> 00:20:12,870
"Congratulations on your big break."

423
00:20:43,950 --> 00:20:44,990
Hello?

424
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:47,820
Monica, it's Joey.

425
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:47,820
Hey, Joey.

426
00:20:48,030 --> 00:20:50,410
Aw, you remember me even though you're a big star.

427
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:53,960
Aw, come on. It'll be years before I forget you.

428
00:20:55,830 --> 00:20:57,750
Joey, what's it like on a movie set, huh?

429
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,750
Do you have a dressing room? Do you have a chair with your name on it?

430
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,800
Uh, yeah, yeah, I got all that going on.

431
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:07,050
Listen, uh, make sure you tell Chandler he couldn't have been more wrong.

432
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:10,720
Uh-oh, I gotta go, Monica. My, uh, sushi's here.

433
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:17,770
Sorry about that. Thanks for waiting. Okay.

434
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:19,810
Everybody smile.

435
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:21,980
Okay.

436
00:21:22,150 --> 00:21:27,110
Thanks a lot. Enjoy your stay at Caesar's. We hope it's toga-rific.

437
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:31,280
Ugh. Kill me. Kill me now.

438
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:40,080
Hey, Rach, can you pass me the TV Guide?

439
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:40,080
Yeah.

440
00:21:40,250 --> 00:21:41,710
Go!

441
00:21:40,250 --> 00:21:41,710
Aah!

442
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:45,300
What are you doing? Get off! Oh, my God!

443
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:47,630
Hold it open. Okay.

444
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:47,630
Aah!

445
00:21:53,810 --> 00:21:56,310
We'll see you in about three or four hours.

